content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line (chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite)",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: 7.1 mm/s RMS at the drive-end bearing housing. The applicable limit is HF-300 Figure 3. 7.1 mm/s is exactly the Zone C / Zone D boundary. Zone C (4.5-7.1) means 'Restricted - plan maintenance'. Zone D (7.1-11.0) means 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The figure does not say which zone a boundary value belongs to. This plan conservatively treats the reading as Zone D, the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Under the site rule SSP-07, vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone requires stopping the machine immediately and notifying the reliability engineer before restart. With the reading treated as Zone D, the pump must be stopped now.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature: 72 C, measured on the housing surface. The applicable limits are in the HF-300 specification table: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading is 2 C above normal but 8 C below alarm. The SSP-07 priority-1 trigger (above the manufacturer's alarm limit) is therefore not met on temperature alone. P1 priority here comes from the vibration stop requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal: no leakage was reported. The 'Leakage at shaft seal' symptom does not apply, so seal replacement is not required on condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only the drive-end housing reading was reported. The manual requires vibration on both bearing housings, with the highest reading classified against Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear. It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and both symptoms are present at the drive end.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is also listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation (insufficient NPSH).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing. It is a listed cause of elevated bearing temperature and may explain the 72 C reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Stop P-103 immediately. Notify the reliability engineer. Do not restart without the reliability engineer's agreement.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Before shutdown, if it can be done safely without delaying the stop, take a vibration reading on the non-drive-end housing as well. Record the highest reading against Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Apply isolation:\n- Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC.\n- Close and lock the suction and discharge valves.\n- Obtain a line-break permit.\n- Drain and vent the pump before opening.\nWear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves, because the line is hypochlorite dosed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Check the grease quantity in the bearing housings for over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Correct the alignment if it is out of tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. Inspect both bearings (DE 6312-C3, NDE 6310-C3) for wear and noise. If either shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both as a pair (procedure 5.3).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. If the back pull-out assembly is removed, use certified lifting equipment under a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor. The assembly weighs 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "8. Inspect the impeller (HF3-210) for damage or imbalance. Check NPSH for cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "9. If the seal is disturbed or must be replaced, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450. Tighten the gland nut to 30 Nm. Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "10. If the casing is opened, fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. Tighten all other fasteners to Table 5 of the manual (values not available in this evidence).",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "11. Re-check laser alignment after any work that moved the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "12. Before restart, confirm the seal flush (Plan 11 from pump discharge) and that the pump is fully primed, so the seal never runs dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "13. With reliability engineer approval, restart and re-measure vibration on both housings. Confirm the readings are below 7.1 mm/s and the bearing housing temperature is at or below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Fit if bearing inspection shows wear; replace as a pair with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Replace as a pair with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, superseding HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above. Contingency only, if the seal is disturbed or damaged.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency only, if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately; it is treated as being in the manufacturer's highest vibration zone. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit; drain and vent first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. P-103 is on a sodium hypochlorite dosed line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, which exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the seal dry; confirm the Plan 11 flush before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians, if inspection confirms wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement (contingency only): 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal part:\n- The O&M manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, fastened per Table 5.\n- Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes this for serial HF3-22000 and above: do not fit HF3-450; use cartridge seal HF3-450B with 30 Nm gland torque (was 25 Nm).\nP-103 is serial HF3-22410, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies to this asset. Use HF3-450B at 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft sleeve:\n- Manual procedure 5.2 says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring.\n- SB-2026-014 adds a replacement criterion of scoring deeper than 0.1 mm for serial HF3-22000 and above.\nThe bulletin criterion applies to HF3-22410.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Figure 3 does not say whether a reading of exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS falls in Zone C or Zone D. This plan treats it as Zone D (stop). The reliability engineer should confirm the classification and the restart criteria.",
    "The non-drive-end housing vibration reading was not reported. The manual requires classifying the highest reading of both housings.",
    "Table 5 fastener torque values (casing, impeller nut, bearing housing) are not included in the evidence. Only the HF3-450B gland nut torque (30 Nm) is known.",
    "Grease type, correct grease quantity and regreasing interval are not given in the evidence.",
    "Section 5.3 gives no step-by-step bearing removal method. It is not stated whether the back pull-out assembly or the seal must be disturbed to change bearings, so seal and sleeve replacement remain contingencies.",
    "Site NPSH available/required data for checking cavitation are not provided.",
    "No standard labour time is given for diagnostic inspection (grease check, impeller inspection, NPSH check).",
    "The revision date of manual AQ-OM-300 Rev D is not given, so it cannot be confirmed whether the manual already reflects SB-2026-014. The bulletin is applied based on the serial range."
  ]
}
